# OpenTide tracking is GitHub-only

Never use Linear for OpenTide work. All OpenTide planning, issues, RFCs, and implementation tracking is **public on GitHub**.

Do **not**:

- Create, update, comment on, or search Linear issues for OpenTideHQ work
- Mirror GitHub issues into Linear
- Put Linear URLs in specs, RFCs, PR bodies, or GitHub issue bodies
- Call Linear MCP tools (`save_issue`, `save_comment`, etc.) while working in this repository or `OpenTideHQ/opentide`

Do:

- Open GitHub issues in [OpenTideHQ/specifications](https://github.com/OpenTideHQ/specifications) for spec/RFC work (use `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/spec-change.yml`)
- Open GitHub issues in [OpenTideHQ/opentide](https://github.com/OpenTideHQ/opentide) for implementation follow-up
- Link those GitHub URLs from RFCs and PRs

A Linear MCP server may be available in the agent environment. Ignore it for OpenTide. SuperTide/private Linear work is out of scope for this repository.
